\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  Glorious things of thee are spoken,\cf0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  Zion, city of our God;
\par  He whose word cannot be broken
\par  Formed thee for His own abode.
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs24 
\par On the Rock of Ages founded,
\par  What can shake thy sure repose?
\par  With salvation's walls surrounded,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Thou mayst smile at all thy foes.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. See! The streams of living waters,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Springing from eternal love,
\par Well supply thy sons and daughters,
\par And all fear of want remove.
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs24 
\par Who can faint while such a river
\par Ever flows their thirst to assuage,-
\par \pard\li45\sl190\slmult0\cf1    \cf0 Grace, which, like the Lord the Giver,
\par    Never fails from age to age?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Round each habitation hovering,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 See! The cloud and fire appear,
\par For a glory and a covering,
\par Showing that the Lord is near.
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs24 
\par Blest inhabitants of Zion,
\par Washed in the Redeemer's blood,
\par Jesus, whom their souls rely on,
\par Makes them kings and priest to God
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Saviour, if a Zion's city
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 I, through grace, a member am,
\par Let the world deride or pity,
\par I will glory in Thy name.
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs24 
\par Fading is the worlding's pleasure,
\par All his boasted pomp and show;
\par Solid joys and lasting treasure
\par \pard      None but Zion's children know.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

